04	Display.Conversation	Manor_Steward	You there! Forgive an old man for shouting: I'm not allowed any nearer. Ambrose, steward of Redrock Manor these fifty years. Well. Steward of the road outside it, these three months.	What happened?	05	Good day to you.	24
05	Display.Conversation	Manor_Steward	Bandits. They came in the spring and threw me out by my collar. The old lord, rest him, was a careful man: he built that house so no thief could ever find his way about it. Rooms with no doors. Stairs to nowhere. It took me twenty years to learn it, and I still go the long way round to the kitchen.\They've never found the vault. I can hear them swearing about it from here.	And you want something from it.	06
06	Display.Conversation	Manor_Steward	The family's signet: a ruby in gold, the Redrock seal. If the young master ever comes home, he'll want it, and I'll not have it melted down by a man called Spleen. Bring it to me and you'll be paid. The rest of the old lord's things in there are yours, with my blessing.	I'll bring it back.	07	Not today.	24
